From: GloriousEggroll <gloriouseggroll@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 12:00:00 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] winewayland: Animate animated cursors.

winewayland only read the first frame of a cursor, so game-supplied
animated cursors (.ani) were static, while winex11 hands every frame and
its delay to Xcursor.

Render every step of an animated cursor into its own buffer when the
cursor is set, and have a helper thread attach them to the cursor surface
in turn, at each frame's delay. The thread only uses the prerendered
buffers and Wayland objects, under the pointer mutex. It idles while the
pointer is outside our windows, while a system cursor shape is in use,
and for static cursors.

https://github.com/GloriousEggroll/proton-ge-custom/issues/919
---
